thaumicdabblery.research.mysticBranch.page1=A quick way to end any given duel is to disarm your opponent. No form of combat demonstrates this fact better than when witches and warlocks cross branches.<BR>Indeed, such encounters are often drawn to a swift conclusion by whoever manages to cast first. To prevent such a scenario from happening to you, you've drafted up a new self-infusion to ensure that you will always have the upper hand.<BR>It took some... esoteric modifications of the circle ritual to make it function with your curative vat instead, but the results are very promising: by merging a witches' magically inclined hands
thaumicdabblery.research.mysticBranch.page2=into your new body and applying the same process used to treat a branch to its fingers, it becomes possible to start utilizing symbological magic while carrying no branch at all. Simply extend your index out and start drawing the same shapes into the air that you would otherwise.<BR>The magic cast via your new mystic hands will, of course, draw on your soul's attuned energy as an ordinary mystic branch would.<BR>Do not try to deflect spells by flicking your wrist. It will not work and you will look like a fool.<BR>With this infusion, you've noticed certain... twitches. It's likely just an odd reflex but you've felt your fingers gravitate towards the nearest cauldron at all times. Huh.
